# NC.6: reconstruction and rational-point output ownership

This file is not the roadmap and is not exhaustive. The definitive document is
research/blueprint/readmes/AnabelianGeometryAndNonabelianChabauty--NC.6.md.

NC.6 is a process-only stage proposed for removal. It introduces no mathematical
declarations, imports, example assertions or replacement supplier structures.
Consequently there are no admitted signatures or definition tests in this file.

Actual reconstruction belongs to NC.1; unipotent groups/comparisons to NC.2;
geometric Selmer varieties to NC.3; iterated-integral maps and general
Chabauty-Kim loci to NC.4; quadratic height equations/loci to NC.5.
EffectiveDiophantineMethods ED.6 owns finite precision certificates, exhaustive
root/disc coverage and comparison with exact global points, using ED.5 exclusions.

The reader's export table and the packet's supplierExports name the 24 existing
nodes. In particular, NC.4/iterated-coordinates uses the right-path period
I(b,x) inverse times gamma(x); NC.4/kim-loci keeps crystalline witnesses,
de Rham period images and reduced geometric image closures distinct.
NC.5/rank-picard-criterion uses rational Neron-Severi rank and its stated
Mordell-Weil cut; NC.5/away-height-constants uses negative away-place sums.
These are supplier conventions to preserve, not new NC.6 signatures.

Section-conjecture surjectivity and eventual Chabauty-Kim equality remain
conjectural at their mathematical owners. Conditional inputs stay conditional.
A finite local locus is not a certified global rational-point enumeration.

Coverage remains partial until independent restructuring acceptance drops NC.6.
Once that accepted result enters the checker registry, this packet can close;
the maintainer applies the stage and edge removals separately.
Elaborating this comment-only companion checks syntax only. It supplies no
elaboration or proof evidence for any supplier theorem or computation.
